# Forms

Applies to `design/` mockups and `frontend/` production UI.

## Placeholders

- Every text-like input (`text`, `search`, `email`, `tel`, `url`, `number`, `password`, `textarea`) must have a **placeholder**.
- Every form `<select>` must show a disabled first option as the placeholder hint (except controls that always have a value selected, e.g. pagination page-size).
- Placeholders are hints, not substitutes for visible `<label>` elements.
- Use i18n — do not hardcode a single language.
- Do not put real or demo passwords in placeholders.

### Placeholder pattern

Derive copy from the field's **translated label** (`{label}`):

| Control | th | en |
|---------|----|----|
| input / text-like | กรุณากรอก{label} | Please enter {label} |
| select | กรุณาเลือก{label} | Please select {label} |
| **search** (`type="search"`) | **ค้นหา** | **Search** |

Template keys: `form.placeholder.input`, `form.placeholder.select` (with `{label}` param). Search uses **`search.placeholder`** only — not the input template.

- **Design:** form fields → `data-i18n-placeholder-input="labelKey"` or `data-i18n-placeholder-select="labelKey"`; **search inputs** → `data-i18n-placeholder="search.placeholder"` + fallback `placeholder="ค้นหา"`; or derive form fields in JS via `i18n.fieldPlaceholder(kind, labelKey)` (see `js/i18n/i18n.js`, `crud-list.js` `fieldHtml`)
- **Frontend:** `placeholder={t('form.placeholder.input', { label: t(labelKey) })}` via next-intl; select → disabled `<SelectItem value="">` or equivalent with `t('form.placeholder.select', { label: t(labelKey) })`
- Legacy explicit keys (`data-i18n-placeholder="key"`) are allowed but prefer the pattern above.

## Phone (`type="tel"`)

- Allowed characters: digits `0-9` and hyphen `-` only (e.g. `02-1234567`, `081-2345678`).
- Attributes: `type="tel"`, `inputmode="tel"`, `autocomplete="tel"`.
- **Design:** filter on input/paste via `telInput.bind(formRoot)` from `js/components/tel-input.js` after every render that rebuilds the DOM.
- **Frontend:** same convention — strip non-digit/non-hyphen on change/paste in the shared `Input` (when implementing frontend forms).

## Password visibility

- Every `type="password"` field must have an eye / eye-off toggle to show and hide the value.
- **Design:** Lucide `eye` / `eye-off` in `design/assets/icons/`; wrap in `.password-field` + `passwordToggle.bind(form)` from `js/components/password-toggle.js`
- **Frontend:** shadcn `Input` + Lucide `Eye` / `EyeOff` from `lucide-react`
- Toggle must update `aria-label` (and `aria-pressed` in design) for accessibility.

## Required fields

- Required inputs show a red `*` after the label text (`aria-hidden="true"` on the asterisk).
- Keep HTML `required` / schema validation — the asterisk is visual only.
- Color: fixed error red (`#dc2626`), not the primary theme color.

## Validation errors

- On save/submit, each empty required field shows an i18n error **under that field** (e.g. `error.required`).
- Do not use a single form-level banner as the only empty-required feedback.
- Clear the field error when the user starts typing again.
- Form-level errors are for non-field failures only (e.g. wrong credentials, server errors).
- Reserve fixed space for errors (`.form-field__error-slot` with `min-height`) so showing/hiding errors does not shift inputs.

## Form leave button (create vs edit)

- **Create** (no record id): label `crud.back` — th: ย้อนกลับ, en: Back
- **Edit** (has record id): label `crud.cancel` — th: ยกเลิก, en: Cancel
- Applies to: full-page form toolbar and CRUD form modal primary dismiss/leave control
- Does NOT apply to: nested sub-modals (contact/bank) or confirm/delete dialogs — those stay `crud.cancel`
- **Design:** set `data-i18n` dynamically from `editId` / `isEdit` at render time
- **Frontend:** same rule when implementing production forms

## Markup pattern (design)

```html
<div class="form-field">
  <label for="field-id">
    <span data-i18n="form.field">Label</span>
    <span class="form-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
  </label>
  <input id="field-id" required data-i18n-placeholder-input="form.field" placeholder="กรุณากรอก…" />
  <div class="form-field__error-slot" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="form-field__error" hidden role="alert"></p>
  </div>
</div>
```

Password fields wrap the input in `.password-field` with a `.password-field__toggle` button.

## FK / parent pickers (Combobox)

When a form field picks one row from a **paginated list API**, use [`RemoteComboboxField`](../../frontend/components/molecules/remote-combobox-field.tsx) with debounced server `search` — see [combobox.mdc](combobox.mdc). Placeholder: `form.placeholder.select` with `{ label }`. Resolve the selected id’s label via get-by-id or pinned options when it is not in the current result page.
